# @coordiation/postcss

Official PostCSS 8 adapter for Coordiation CSS. It scans configured source roots, replaces `@coordiation` with static framework output, reports scanner diagnostics through PostCSS warnings, and registers file plus directory dependencies with compatible runners.

## Install

```sh
pnpm add -D postcss @coordiation/css @coordiation/postcss
```

## Configure

```js
// postcss.config.mjs
import coordiation from "@coordiation/postcss";

export default {
  plugins: [
    coordiation({
      content: ["src"],
      cwd: process.cwd()
    })
  ]
};
```

Place Coordiation before Autoprefixer or minification plugins so downstream plugins receive the generated CSS.

## Input

```css
@coordiation;

@co-theme {
  --co-color-brand-500: oklch(62.3% 0.214 259.815);
}
```

Only stylesheets containing a top-level `@coordiation` marker are transformed. Other CSS files pass through unchanged, which makes the adapter safe in multi-entry PostCSS pipelines.

## Dependencies and warnings

- Every scanned source file produces a PostCSS `dependency` message.
- Every configured source directory produces a recursive `dir-dependency` message so runners can rebuild when files are added or removed.
- Dynamic-class and unsupported-candidate diagnostics use `result.warn()` and appear through the runner's standard warning channel.
- The plugin is asynchronous and preserves ordinary PostCSS source-map processing.

Use complete literal `co-` class names in scanned source. Dynamic concatenation cannot be discovered reliably; use a safelist when the set is finite.
